# Dering corpus sweep data
#
# Generated by: cargo run --release -p zenjpeg --example dering_corpus_sweep -- \
#     --max-photos 25 --max-graphics 10 \
#     --out /mnt/v/output/zenjpeg/dering_sweep.csv
#
# Branch: investigate/q10-baseline-gap
# Commit: 71bcdaa4bcaabf221d8019fe1650117c643a3c1f
# Date: 2026-04-14
# Host: Ryzen 9 7950X (WSL2)
#
# Columns: category,name,width,height,q,dering,bytes,ssim2,encode_ms
# Q levels: 10, 30, 50, 70, 85, 95
# Dering: true (default) vs false (via EncoderConfig::deringing(false))
# Encoder: YCbCr 4:2:0 (ChromaSubsampling::Quarter), baseline (non-progressive)
# Decoder: zune-jpeg (bench_utils::decode_jpeg_to_rgb)
# Metric: fast_ssim2::compute_ssimulacra2 (0..100, higher better)
#
# Corpora:
#   frymire: 1 image from zenjpeg/tests/images/frymire.png (classic screenshot)
#   photo: first 25 alphabetical PNGs from CID22/CID22-512/training
#   graphic: all 10 screenshots from codec-corpus/gb82-sc
